sentences.l:
“Othryoneus, beyond all mortals indeed I commend you,
if truly indeed you will fulfil everything that you undertook
to Dardanus’ descendant Priam;

And he fell, as when an oak falls, or a white poplar,
or a tall pine, which on the mountains builders
cut down with newly sharpened axes, to be ship-timber;

for he was hidden under the shield equal on every side,
which he, then, with hides of oxen and flashing bronze
kept carrying, round-wrought, fitted with two bars;

under which all of him was hemmed in, and it flew over, the bronze spear,
and dry his shield rang, as it ran over it,
the spear;

and the eldest of the daughters he had married, Hippodameia,
whom exceedingly at heart loved her father and her lady mother
in the hall;

And he fell with a thud, and the spear in his heart was fixed,
which, gasping for him, even the butt-end shook
of the spear;

Strange man, but also yourself stand opposite me,
so that you may see what sort of offspring of Zeus I come here,
who first begot Minos, guardian for Crete;

and Minos in turn begot a blameless son, Deucalion,
and Deucalion me begot for many men a lord,
in broad Crete;
